# The sandbox image's build context is this directory (workers/yak/wrangler.toml
# `image_build_context`), and all it needs is the Deno workspace the `yak` CLI
# resolves in (workers/yak/sandbox/Dockerfile). So everything is out, then the
# workspace config, packages/, and the members outside packages/ are let back
# in, since deno refuses a workspace with a member missing. Wrangler pipes the
# Dockerfile on stdin, so this file has to sit at the context root rather than
# beside the Dockerfile.
*
!deno.json
!deno.lock
!packages
!workers/yak/deno.json
!apps/vale/deno.json

# Never into the image, wherever they turn up under what was let in.
**/.env*
**/.dev.vars*
**/node_modules
**/.wrangler
**/*_test.ts
